Subject: [PATCH] arm64: uapi: key __BITS_PER_LONG on __LP64__

As ../kernel/patches/0006 for 3.10, which this kernel needs as much: the ROM's
build stopped in the 32-bit half of the audio HAL with "format specifies type
'ssize_t' (aka 'int') but the argument has type 'ssize_t' (aka 'long')".
LineageOS exports these headers once, for arm64, ahead of bionic's own, to 32-bit
compiles too, and an unconditional 64 makes ssize_t a long there. GCC and clang
define __LP64__ for LP64 targets only.
---
--- arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h
+++ arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h
@@ -16,7 +16,17 @@
 #ifndef __ASM_BITSPERLONG_H
 #define __ASM_BITSPERLONG_H
 
+/*
+ * These headers are exported once, for arm64, and the Android build hands the same
+ * copy to its 32-bit compiles too. An unconditional 64 then makes ssize_t a long in
+ * 32-bit code. __LP64__ is defined by GCC and clang for LP64 targets only, so key the
+ * width on that and the header is right for both ABIs.
+ */
+#ifdef __LP64__
 #define __BITS_PER_LONG 64
+#else
+#define __BITS_PER_LONG 32
+#endif
 
 #include <asm-generic/bitsperlong.h>
 
